@startuml
' Figure 4‑3 Sequence diagram for Use Case 3: Post Reply
actor "Registered Student User" as RSU
participant "MUSTHub System" as S
participant "u1 : User" as U
participant "p1 : Post" as P1
participant "r_new : Reply" as RNEW
participant "Local File System" as LFS

RSU -> S : replyToPost(postId)
activate S

S -> U : checkLoginStatus()
activate U
alt [loggedIn == false]
S -> S : reject operation, show prompt
deactivate S
else [loggedIn == true]
U --> S : loggedIn = true
deactivate U

S -> LFS : readPostData()
activate LFS
LFS --> S : target post record
deactivate LFS

S -> RSU : requestReplyText()
RSU --> S : reply‑text

S -> S : validateNotEmpty(reply‑text)
note over S : <<include>> Sensitive Word Filtering
S -> S : sensitiveWordCheck()

alt [empty reply]
S -> S : prompt for re‑input
else [sensitive word hit]
S -> S : show matched keyword, store nothing
else [check pass]
S -> RNEW : createReplyObj()
S -> LFS : saveReplyData(replyObj)
activate LFS
LFS --> S : acknowledge save success
deactivate LFS

S -> P1 : replyCount +=1 ; lastActivityAt = now
note over P1 : If p1.status = DOWNGRADED\n  reportCount <3 → T3 set VISIBLE\n  reportCount ≥3 → T5 set FLAGGED\n  call savePostData(postObj) to persist
S --> RSU : show success feedback
end alt
end alt

' Exception
alt [fileReadError]
S -> S : show error message, abort this reply
else [fileWriteError]
S -> S : show error prompt;\nreplyCount and post status remain unchanged
end alt
deactivate S
@enduml
